# Pre-change world saves, kept for hard rule 1's load test. They are real Minecraft worlds — a
# megabyte each and binary — and they belong to a session rather than to the repository. Session 06's
# archives were lost and 07 had to rebuild one from a detached checkout; 08's lived in a scratchpad
# and were gone by 09. Keeping them here means the next session can find them, and this line means
# they never reach a commit.
/.archives/
